WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:15.042
Hi! In synthesis, you join two sentences into one. In transformation, you rewrite a sentence in a new way. The most important rule is that the meaning must stay the same. Let's learn how.

2
00:00:15.192 --> 00:00:20.154
It was raining, but they still played football. That is unexpected.

3
00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:25.914
With although: although it was raining, they played football. Don't add but as well.

4
00:00:26.064 --> 00:00:33.954
Because gives a reason, so gives a result, unless means if not, and until means up to that time.

5
00:00:34.104 --> 00:00:39.114
Use who for people, which for things, and whose to show who something belongs to.

6
00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:47.874
Both sentences are about the girl. Joined: the girl who won the race is my cousin. We drop she.

7
00:00:48.024 --> 00:00:54.546
The box is too heavy for me to carry can become: the box is so heavy that I cannot carry it.

8
00:00:54.696 --> 00:01:02.490
Ali can sing. Ali can dance. This becomes: Ali can both sing and dance.

9
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.218
Watch out! Writing she after who repeats the same person!

10
00:01:07.368 --> 00:01:11.250
Who already takes the place of she, so we remove she.

11
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.562
After joining, always read the whole sentence to check for extra words.

12
00:01:17.712 --> 00:01:28.146
Your turn! I lost a bag. The bag was red. Join them with which. Pause and think.

13
00:01:28.296 --> 00:01:34.554
The answer is: the bag which I lost was red. Did you get it right?

14
00:01:34.704 --> 00:01:45.186
Another one! Sam was tired. He kept running. Begin with although. Pause and think.

15
00:01:45.336 --> 00:01:51.954
The answer is: although Sam was tired, he kept running. Did you get it right?

16
00:01:52.104 --> 00:02:02.898
Next one! The man helped us. His car was blue. Join them with whose. Pause and think.

17
00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:11.682
The answer is: the man whose car was blue helped us. Whose takes the place of his. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:11.832 --> 00:02:22.194
One more! The soup is too hot for me to drink. Rewrite it with so and that. Pause and think.

19
00:02:22.344 --> 00:02:33.018
The answer is: the soup is so hot that I cannot drink it. The meaning is the same. Don't forget the word it at the end. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:33.168 --> 00:02:43.914
Last one! Mei can swim. Mei can cycle. Join them with both and and. Pause and think.

21
00:02:44.064 --> 00:02:50.370
The answer is: Mei can both swim and cycle. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:59.082
Remember: choose the right connector. Use who for people, which for things and whose for belonging, and remove the extra pronoun.

23
00:02:59.232 --> 00:03:05.778
When you transform a sentence, the meaning must stay the same. Read the whole sentence when you finish.

24
00:03:05.928 --> 00:03:10.602
Today, try using who to describe a friend!

